Title: Fix crash on startup when config file missing

Description: This PR addresses a null pointer dereference that occurs when the application starts without a configuration file. Added a fallback to default settings and updated the ConfigLoader class.

Changes:
- src/main/java/com/example/ConfigLoader.java
```diff
@@ -12,7 +12,12 @@ public class ConfigLoader {
    public Config load() {
-        File configFile = new File(path);
-        String content = Files.readString(configFile.toPath());
+        File configFile = new File(path);
+        if (!configFile.exists()) {
+            // Use default configuration when file is missing
+            return Config.defaultConfig();
+        }
+        String content = Files.readString(configFile.toPath());
        return parse(content);
    }
```
- Added unit test `ConfigLoaderTest.testLoadDefaultWhenMissing` in src/test/java/com/example/ConfigLoaderTest.java.

Testing:
1. Delete `config.yml` from the project root.
2. Run `mvn test`.
3. Verify that the test passes and the application starts without throwing an exception.

This resolves issue #342.

