Title: Fix incorrect handling of null values in UserService#getUserProfile

Description:
The current implementation of `UserService#getUserProfile` throws a `NullPointerException` when the `userId` argument is null, which violates the API contract that a missing userId should result in a 400 Bad Request response. This issue was reproduced during integration testing of the new authentication flow.

Steps to Reproduce:
1. Call the endpoint `GET /api/users/profile` without providing the `userId` query parameter.
2. Observe a 500 Internal Server Error in the response.
3. Check the server logs – a NullPointerException is printed.

Proposed Changes:
- Add a null check for `userId` at the beginning of the method.
- Return `ResponseEntity.badRequest().body("userId is required")` when null.
- Update unit tests to cover the null case.

Existing Code (before change):
```java
public UserProfile getUserProfile(String userId) {
    User user = userRepository.findById(userId).orElseThrow(NotFoundException::new);
    return mapper.toProfile(user);
}
```

New Code (after change):
```java
public ResponseEntity<?> getUserProfile(String userId) {
    if (userId == null) {
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body("userId is required");
    }
    User user = userRepository.findById(userId).orElseThrow(NotFoundException::new);
    UserProfile profile = mapper.toProfile(user);
    return ResponseEntity.ok(profile);
}
```

