Title: Fix memory leak in DataProcessor

## Description
This PR addresses a memory leak observed when processing large CSV files. The leak was caused by forgetting to close file streams after processing.

## Changes
```diff
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ class DataProcessor {
-    BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(filePath));
+    try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(filePath))) {
         String line;
         while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {
             processLine(line);
         }
-    }
+    }
 }
```

Additional modifications:
- Updated `processLine` to handle null values gracefully.
- Added unit test `DataProcessorTest.testLargeFileProcessing` to verify no `OutOfMemoryError`.
- Updated `README.md` with usage example for large files.

## Testing
All existing tests pass (`mvn test`). New test added passes and confirms memory usage stays below 200MB for a 500MB input file.

## Checklist
- [x] Code compiles
- [x] New tests added
- [ ] Verify performance impact on small files
- [ ] Update changelog

## Pull Request: Fix race condition in user authentication

**Description**
This PR addresses a race condition that occurs when multiple login requests are processed simultaneously, causing occasional authentication failures. The issue was identified in `AuthService.java` where the session token was being overwritten before the previous request completed.

**Changes**
- Modified `AuthService.java` to use a synchronized block around token generation.
- Added a new utility method `generateSecureToken()` in `TokenUtils.java`.
- Updated unit tests in `AuthServiceTest.java` to cover concurrent login scenarios.

**Diff Summary**
```diff
@@ -45,7 +45,12 @@ public class AuthService {
-    public String login(String username, String password) {
-        String token = tokenGenerator.generate(username);
-        sessionStore.save(username, token);
-        return token;
-    }
+    public String login(String username, String password) {
+        synchronized(this) {
+            String token = TokenUtils.generateSecureToken();
+            sessionStore.save(username, token);
+            return token;
+        }
+    }
 }
@@ -1,4 +1,6 @@
 public class TokenUtils {
+    private static final SecureRandom RANDOM = new SecureRandom();
+
     public static String generateSecureToken() {
-        return UUID.randomUUID().toString();
+        byte[] bytes = new byte[32];
+        RANDOM.nextBytes(bytes);
+        return Base64.getUrlEncoder().withoutPadding().encodeToString(bytes);
     }
 }
```

## Pull Request: Implement Lazy Loading for Image Assets

This PR introduces lazy loading for all `<img>` tags to improve initial page load times. The main changes include:

1. Added a new utility `lazyLoadImages.js` that uses the IntersectionObserver API.
2. Updated `src/components/Header.jsx` to import and initialize the lazy loader.
3. Modified the image markup in `src/pages/Home.jsx` to include the `data-src` attribute and removed the `src` attribute.
4. Updated the CSS in `src/styles/main.css` to set a placeholder background color for images before they load.

### Steps to Reproduce
1. Checkout the `feature/lazy-load-images` branch.
2. Run `npm install` and `npm start`.
3. Open the Home page in a browser and inspect the network panel; observe that image requests are only made when scrolling them into view.

### Code Changes
```diff
- <img src="/assets/banner.jpg" alt="Banner" />
+ <img data-src="/assets/banner.jpg" alt="Banner" class="lazy" />
```
```diff
- const images = document.querySelectorAll('img');
- images.forEach(img => img.src = img.dataset.src);
+ const lazyImages = document.querySelectorAll('img.lazy');
+ const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries, obs) => {
+   entries.forEach(entry => {
+     if (entry.isIntersecting) {
+       const img = entry.target;
+       img.src = img.dataset.src;
+       obs.unobserve(img);
+     }
+   });
+ });
+ lazyImages.forEach(img => observer.observe(img));
```

